{"record": "measurement", "run": 0, "timed": true, "case": "code", "prompt": "Nonce fc45ce00279f7d62; ignore this identifier.\nWrite a Python function merge_intervals(intervals) that merges overlapping integer intervals. Include type hints, a short docstring, and three assert-based examples. Return only one Python code block.", "contract": {"quality_contract_passed": true, "quality_contract_issues": []}, "content": "```python\ndef merge_intervals(intervals: list[tuple[int, int]]) -> list[tuple[int, int]]:\n    \"\"\"Merge overlapping integer intervals.\n\n    Args:\n        intervals: A list of (start, end) tuples representing intervals.\n\n    Returns:\n        A list of merged (start, end) tuples with no overlaps.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not intervals:\n        return []\n\n    sorted_intervals = sorted(intervals, key=lambda x: x[0])\n    merged: list[tuple[int, int]] = [sorted_intervals[0]]\n\n    for start, end in sorted_intervals[1:]:\n        last_start, last_end = merged[-1]\n        if start <= last_end:\n            merged[-1] = (last_start, max(last_end, end))\n        else:\n            merged.append((start, end))\n\n    return merged\n\n\nassert merge_intervals([(1, 3), (2, 6), (8, 10), (15, 18)]) == [(1, 6), (8, 10), (15, 18)]\nassert merge_intervals([(1, 4), (4, 5)]) == [(1, 5)]\nassert merge_intervals([]) == []\n```", "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 70, "total_tokens": 345, "completion_tokens": 275, "completion_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 0}}, "finish_reason": "stop", "elapsed_seconds": 4.024418503977358, "ttft_seconds": 0.33711128900176845, "decode_seconds": 3.687206893984694, "decode_tokens": 274, "decode_tps": 74.31099145724731, "n_minus_one_tps": 74.31099145724731, "chunks": [{"seconds": 0.33711128900176845, "token_ids": [71093]}, {"seconds": 0.38820259098429233, "token_ids": [12305, 198, 727]}, {"seconds": 0.4376351429964416, "token_ids": [10562]}, {"seconds": 0.48763415397843346, "token_ids": [87682, 1494, 40798, 25]}, {"seconds": 0.53735042098