{"record": "measurement", "run": 0, "timed": true, "case": "fable", "prompt": "Nonce d114b1d9d0eadf46; ignore this identifier.\nWrite a self-contained fable of 140 to 170 words about two parrots who disagree about sharing credit. End with a one-sentence moral.", "contract": {"quality_contract_passed": false, "quality_contract_issues": ["fable has 173 words, outside 140..170"]}, "content": "In the vibrant canopy of the Emerald Jungle, lived two parrots, Pip and Pop. They were inseparable partners in a grand performance, singing harmonious duets that drew crowds from miles away. One afternoon, a wealthy merchant arrived, offering a golden cage for the bird with the most beautiful voice. Pip, eager for the prize, claimed sole credit for their success. \"My high notes were the highlight,\" he squawked proudly. Pop, offended by the betrayal, retorted, \"Without my steady rhythm, your notes would have been chaotic noise.\"\n\nThe merchant, confused by their bickering, decided neither deserved the reward. He left without buying either bird. Pip and Pop sat in silence, realizing their greed had cost them both the prize and their harmony. They had forgotten that their beauty lay in their unity, not their individual talents. The golden cage remained empty, a stark reminder of their foolishness. They returned to their branch, singing together once more, but the memory of the lost opportunity lingered.\n\nTrue success is found in shared effort, not individual glory.", "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 68, "total_tokens": 290, "completion_tokens": 222, "completion_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 0}}, "finish_reason": "stop", "elapsed_seconds": 5.106017726007849, "ttft_seconds": 0.1594720520079136, "decode_seconds": 4.946471411996754, "decode_tokens": 221, "decode_tps": 44.678313406200076, "n_minus_one_tps": 44.678313406200076, "chunks": [{"seconds": 0.1594720520079136, "token_ids": [623]}, {"seconds": 0.20216946999426, "token_ids": [279, 31883, 60847]}, {"seconds": 0.244673587993